        "number": 3,
        "title": "Part 3",
        "sectionHtml": "\n<div class=\"part-header\">\n<p><strong>Part 3</strong></p>\n<p>Questions 21–30</p>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"questions-container\">\n\n<!-- Questions 21–26 -->\n<div class=\"question\">\n<div class=\"question-prompt\">\n<p><strong>Questions 21–26</strong></p>\n<p>Choose the correct letter, <strong>A, B or C</strong>.</p>\n<p class=\"centered-title\">Eyewitness reliability</p>\n</div>\n\n<!-- Q21 -->\n<p><strong>21</strong> Eleanor thinks eyewitnesses are believed when</p>\n<div class=\"multi-choice-question\">\n<div class=\"multi-choice-option\"><label> A they are respected members of the community.</label></div>\n<div class=\"multi-choice-option\"><label> B they make their statements with confidence.</label></div>\n<div class=\"multi-choice-option\"><label> C they use sophisticated language in their accounts.</label></div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- Q22 -->\n<p><strong>22</strong> What concerns Duckie Eleanor and Jamie about the texts they have read so far?</p>\n<div class=\"multi-choice-question\">\n<div class=\"multi-choice-option\"><label> A No clear conclusions are reached</label></div>\n<div class=\"multi-choice-option\"><label> B The studies involved comparatively few people.</label></div>\n<div class=\"multi-choice-option\"><label> C Some of the data were gathered some time ago.</label></div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- Q23 -->\n<p><strong>23</strong> They agree that the most significant factor affecting eyewitness reliability is</p>\n<div class=\"multi-choice-question\">\n<div class=\"multi-choice-option\"><label> A how good the lighting is.</label></div>\n<div class=\"multi-choice-option\"><label> B how long the event lasts.</label></div>\n<div class=\"multi-choice-option\"><label> C how far away the witness is.</label></div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- Q24 -->\n<p><strong>24</strong> Jamie criticises photo-identifications, saying witnesses</p>\n<div class=\"multi-choice-question\">\n<div class=\"multi-choice-option\"><label> A fail to compare the photos with their memory of the event.</label></div>\n<div class=\"multi-choice-option\"><label> B are not properly briefed about the procedure.</label></div>\n<div class=\"multi-choice-option\"><label> C become easily influenced by a figure of authority.</label></div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- Q25 -->\n<p><strong>25</strong> They agree that the term ‘naive observer’ means a person who</p>\n<div class=\"multi-choice-question\">\n<div class=\"multi-choice-option\"><label> A has no experience of a police investigation.</label></div>\n<div class=\"multi-choice-option\"><label> B did not realise they were witnessing a crime.</label></div>\n<div class=\"multi-choice-option\"><label> C was not present at the incident.</label></div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- Q26 -->\n<p><strong>26</strong> They have learned that witnesses are reluctant to change their opinions because</p>\n<div class=\"multi-choice-question\">\n<div class=\"multi-choice-option\"><label> A they do not want to appear foolish.</label></div>\n<div class=\"multi-choice-option\"><label> B they fear the legal consequences.</label></div>\n<div class=\"multi-choice-option\"><label> C they are keen for the case to be concluded.</label></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- Questions 27–30 (Matching) -->\n<div class=\"question\">\n<div class=\"question-prompt\">\n<p><strong>Questions 27–30</strong></p>\n<p>What problem may there be with child witnesses at each of the following stages of an interview?</p>\n<p>Choose <strong>FOUR</strong> answers from the box and write the correct letter, <strong>A–F</strong>, next to questions 27–30.</p>\n</div>\n\n<div>\n<p><strong>Problems with child witnesses</strong></p>\n<p>A frightened by the unfamiliar environment<br>\nB influenced by the interviewer Duckie<br>\nC not understanding the difference between truth and lies<br>\nD unwillingness to say they don’t know<br>\nE confused by the terminology<br>\nF distrust of the interviewer</p>\n</div>\n\n<table class=\"matching-table\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Interview stages</th>\n<th>Answer (A–F)</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>27</strong> Rapport</td>\n<td><div class=\"drop-zone\">Drop here</div></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>28</strong> Open-ended questions</td>\n<td><div class=\"drop-zone\">Drop here</div></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>29</strong> Closed questions</td>\n<td><div class=\"drop-zone\">Drop here</div></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>30</strong> Closure</td>\n<td><div class=\"drop-zone\">Drop here</div></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n<!-- Options for drag-drop -->\n<div class=\"matching-options-list\">\n<div class=\"drag-item\" data-value=\"A\">A frightened by the unfamiliar environment</div>\n<div class=\"drag-item\" data-value=\"B\">B influenced by the interviewer Duckie</div>\n<div class=\"drag-item\" data-value=\"C\">C not understanding the difference between truth and lies</div>\n<div class=\"drag-item\" data-value=\"D\">D unwillingness to say they don’t know</div>\n<div class=\"drag-item\" data-value=\"E\">E confused by the terminology</div>\n<div class=\"drag-item\" data-value=\"F\">F distrust of the interviewer</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n</div>\n",
